<title>USA: Wang Labs Q3 March 31 operating shr profit.</title>
<headline>Wang Labs Q3 March 31 operating shr profit.</headline>
<dateline>BILLERICA, Mass. 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>WANG LABORATORIES INC</p>
<p>				   Qtr Ended 3/31  9 Mos Ended 3/31</p>
<p>				   1997	1996     1997	1996</p>
<p>Revs: Service	     $ 246.8    $ 165.6 $ 698.1    $ 516.9</p>
<p>	Product		  68.3	 82.7   232.1	248.9</p>
<p>Total Revenue		 315.1	248.3   930.2	765.8</p>
<p>Costs and Expenses</p>
<p>  Cost of Service	   193.4	114.9   529.0	352.7</p>
<p>  Cost of Product	    49.5	 54.8   171.0	169.8</p>
<p>  Research &amp; Development    0.9	  0.4     2.8	  3.1</p>
<p>  SG&amp;A			   80.3	 46.9   182.1	143.3</p>
<p>Amortization of Intangibles-</p>
<p>Acquisition and Fresh-start(a)</p>
<p>				   22.7(b)     8.6    42.2 (b)   25.9</p>
<p>Integration-related Costs and Other</p>
<p>	   Charges		8.6 (c)	-    36.0 (d)	-</p>
<p>  Operating Income (Loss) (40.3)	22.7   (32.9)	71.0</p>
<p>Other Income (Expense)</p>
<p>	Interest Expense    (3.9)	(1.3)   (8.8)	(3.5)</p>
<p>	Interest Income	 1.3	  2.0     3.9	  6.8</p>
<p>  Other Income net	  (0.1)	1.2     0.6	  2.7</p>
<p>  Total Other Income	(2.7)	1.9    (4.3)	 6.0</p>
<p>Benefit (Provision) for</p>
<p>     Income Taxes	   21.1	(7.3)    18.1     (28.5)</p>
<p>   Income-Continuing Ops (21.9)(e)    17.3   (19.1) (e) 48.5</p>
<p>   Income-Disc Ops	 101.3     (12.3)    76.6     (57.3)</p>
<p>   Net Income (Loss)	79.4	  5.0    57.5	(8.8)</p>
<p>   Net EPS (Loss)	   1.81     (0.20)    1.23     (0.78)</p>
<p>   EBITDA		    182.9	 33.2   251.3	103.4</p>
<p>	 (Dollars in millions, except per share data)</p>
<p>NOTE: Ongoing services operations, excluding the effect of the software business and the non-recurring charges, contributed $36.2 million to EBITDA and $0.12 to EPS.</p>
<p>(a)  Amortization of acquired intangible assets and assets identified in connection with the adoption of &quot;fresh-start&quot; reporting.</p>
<p>(b)  Includes $14.4M associated with the write down of Bull-related intangibles</p>
<p>(c)  Charges associated with organizational realignment and reductions in G&amp;A infrastructure</p>
<p>(d)  Charges associated with the integration and consolidation initiatives related to the acquisition of I-NET and other cost reduction initiative including reductions in G&amp;A infrastructure.</p>
<p>(e)  Includes the effects of $52.5M pretax ($29.9M post tax) non-recurring charges related to the sale of the software business, organizational realignment and reductions in G&amp;A infrastructure, as well as reductions in the carrying value of certain tangible and intangible assets</p>
